 ### Visits
 
-<a id="req-vis-001"></a><a id="req-vis-002"></a>
+<a id="req-vis-001"></a><a id="req-vis-002"></a><a id="req-vis-003"></a>
 
-A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a short description of what it is for `[REQ-VIS-001]`. When booking, the pet's earlier visits are shown alongside, so whoever is booking can see what has already been done `[REQ-VIS-002]`.
+A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a short description of what it is for `[REQ-VIS-001]`. When booking, the pet's earlier visits are shown alongside, so whoever is booking can see what has already been done `[REQ-VIS-002]`. A booked visit can be corrected afterwards: both the date it is for and its description can be changed, under the same rules that governed the original booking, and the correction replaces the visit rather than adding a second one `[REQ-VIS-003]` (confirmed 2026-08-07). A booked visit still cannot be cancelled — NG-5.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a pet, when a description and a date later than today are supplied, then the visit is recorded and the booking is confirmed.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a blank description, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the description is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the date is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-002]` given a pet with earlier visits, when a new visit is being booked, then those earlier visits are shown with their dates and descriptions.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a booked visit, when it is opened for correction, then it is presented for editing already carrying its current date and description.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a booked visit opened for correction, when a description and a date later than today are supplied, then that same visit carries the new date and description and the pet has gained no further visit.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a booked visit opened for correction, when the correction is accepted, then the owner's record is shown with the corrected visit under its pet.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a correction with a blank description, when it is submitted, then the correction is refused and the description is named.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a correction with a date of today or earlier, when it is submitted, then the correction is refused and the date is named.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a refused correction, when it is redisplayed, then the visit still carries the date and description it had before.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. Booking a visit for a pet that does not belong to the named owner is refused.
 2. The date offered by default is the earliest date that would be accepted.
+3. Correcting a visit that does not exist, or that is not a visit of the named pet, is refused rather than presented as an empty form.
+
+**ADR:** [ADR: Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope, Cancelling Is Not](adr/2026-08-07-non-goal-visit-correction.md)
 
